writeFileSync(aboutPath, layout('About Ellis Services Group', 'about/', `<section class="hero inner">${image(0)}<div class="container hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / PERTH, WESTERN AUSTRALIA</p><h1>ELLIS SERVICES GROUP.</h1><p>Company information, roof and drainage enquiry context, and direct Perth contact details.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Make an enquiry</a></div></section><article class="section"><div class="narrow"><p class="eyebrow">THE COMPANY</p><h2>A clear starting point for roof and drainage enquiries.</h2><p>Ellis Services Group is the public-facing name used on this website for Perth roof repair and drainage enquiries. This page brings together the company record, the website contact details and a practical way to begin a conversation about a property. The service pages are written around visible roofline and water-path details, so an enquiry can begin with what has actually been noticed rather than an assumption about the cause or the scope of work.</p><p>A roof question may start with a water mark, a changed ridge line, a tile that looks out of place, a metal-sheet edge, a flashing junction, a gutter overflow point or a downpipe connection. These are useful observations, but they are not a diagnosis. Recording the location, material and timing of a visible change helps make the first conversation clearer. If it is safe to do so from ground level, photographs can also give useful context for discussing the next step.</p><p>Ellis Services Group provides information across roof repairs, roof leaks, tile roofs, metal roofs, ridge capping and repointing, flashing, gutters, downpipes, roof maintenance, storm-related roof observations and roof inspection enquiries. Each topic has its own page so homeowners, property managers and other enquirers can identify the part of the roofline or drainage route they want to discuss.</p></div></article><section class="section texture"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">COMPANY RECORD</p><h2>Registered entity information.</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Legal entity</h3><p><strong>ELLIS SERVICES GROUP PTY LTD</strong></p><p>Entity type: Australian Private Company.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>ABN and ACN</h3><p>ABN 96 645 821 745</p><p>ACN 645 821 745</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Current ABR status</h3><p>ABN status: Active from 11 November 2020.</p><p>GST registered from 11 November 2020.</p></article></div><p>The company facts above are drawn from the public Australian Business Register record. <a class="text-link" href="https://abr.business.gov.au/ABN/View?id=645821745" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the official ABN Lookup record</a>.</p><p>That record is a company-registration reference. It does not itself provide a licence number, insurer, insurance policy wording or a promise about a particular property outcome. Questions about a specific scope of work can be raised directly before proceeding.</p></div></section><article class="section"><div class="narrow"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE HELP YOU DISCUSS</p><h2>Roofline details, materials and water paths.</h2><p>A roof is made up of connected elements rather than isolated parts. Tiles or metal sheets meet ridges, valleys, flashings, penetrations, gutters and downpipes. A visible change in one place can be easier to explain when the nearby materials and the direction of water flow are also noted. The purpose of the website is to make those starting points easier to recognise and describe in plain language.</p><p>For a roof repair enquiry, it can help to state whether the observation is on a tile roof or metal roof, whether it is near a ridge, valley, flashing or penetration, and whether the change appears on the outside, inside or both. For a drainage enquiry, it can help to identify the gutter section, outlet, downpipe or ground connection involved. A simple description is enough: the aim is not to diagnose the issue before getting in touch.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Roof repairs</h3><p>Use the roof repair pages to organise a question around a visible roof surface, edge, junction or material change.</p><p><a href="/roof-repairs/">Explore roof repairs</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Leak and flashing context</h3><p>Start with where a mark, drip or water-related change appears, and note relevant roof features nearby.</p><p><a href="/roof-leak-repairs/">Explore roof leak repairs</a> · <a href="/flashing-repairs/">Read about flashings</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Gutters and downpipes</h3><p>Trace the visible route from a roof edge to gutter, outlet and downpipe before describing the concern.</p><p><a href="/gutters-downpipes/">Explore gutters and downpipes</a></p></article></div></div></article><section class="section texture"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">HOW AN ENQUIRY IS ARRANGED</p><h2>Bring the useful details together before the conversation begins.</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>01 / Share the location</h3><p>Tell us the property suburb or address, plus the best contact details for the person making the enquiry. The website office address is 140 St Georges Terrace, Perth WA 6000.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>02 / Describe what is visible</h3><p>Explain the roof, drainage or interior detail that prompted the enquiry. Mention the material or location if known, and whether the change followed rain, wind or another event.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>03 / Add photos where helpful</h3><p>Clear photographs taken safely from the ground can help show the general setting. Please do not access a roof or unsafe area simply to collect information.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>04 / Discuss the next step</h3><p>Call, email or use the contact form to begin the conversation. The details provided through the website are general information and do not replace property-specific advice.</p></article></div></div></section><article class="section"><div class="narrow"><p class="eyebrow">CONTACT ELLIS SERVICES GROUP</p><h2>Direct Perth contact details.</h2><p>For a new roof repair, roof leak, gutter, downpipe or roof-maintenance enquiry, use the details below. Including the property location and a short description of the visible concern can make the first response more focused.</p><ul><li><strong>Website office:</strong> 140 St Georges Terrace, Perth WA 6000</li><li><strong>Telephone:</strong> <a href="tel:+61405878406">0405 878 406</a></li><li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:ellisservicesgroup3@outlook.com">ellisservicesgroup3@outlook.com</a></li></ul><p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Send an enquiry</a></p><p>If the matter concerns an immediate safety risk, keep clear of the affected area and contact the relevant emergency service or qualified provider as appropriate. For non-urgent questions, the contact form, telephone number and email address above are the direct routes to Ellis Services Group.</p></div></article><section class="section texture"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">QUESTIONS PEOPLE OFTEN ASK</p><h2>Questions people often ask before contacting us.</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>What should I include in a roof repair enquiry?</summary><p>Start with the property location, the visible detail you noticed, where it appears and when you first saw it. A brief note about nearby roof materials, drainage components or recent weather can add helpful context. You do not need to know the cause before making contact.</p></details><details><summary>Can I ask about gutters or downpipes as well as the roof?</summary><p>Yes. Gutters, outlets and downpipes form part of the visible drainage route from the roof edge. Describe the section that concerns you and what you observe during or after rain where known.</p></details><details><summary>Does the About page list company registration details?</summary><p>Yes. Ellis Services Group Pty Ltd is listed here with ABN 96 645 821 745 and ACN 645 821 745. The official ABN Lookup link is included above so visitors can check the current public record directly.</p></details><details><summary>What does the ABR record confirm?</summary><p>The Australian Business Register entry confirms the entity name, company type, ABN status, GST registration and ACN shown on this page. It is a company-registration record rather than evidence of project-specific scope, insurance cover or licensing.</p></details><details><summary>Where is the website office located?</summary><p>The website office address is 140 St Georges Terrace, Perth WA 6000. For a property enquiry, include the property location separately so the discussion is tied to the correct site.</p></details><details><summary>How can I make contact?</summary><p>Call 0405 878 406, email ellisservicesgroup3@outlook.com or use the website contact form. The service pages can also help you put the visible roof or drainage detail into words before you get in touch.</p></details></div></div></section>`));

